<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Martin steps down as chair of S.Africa's Vodacom.</title>
<headline>Martin steps down as chair of S.Africa's Vodacom.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-06-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Alwyn Martin has resigned as chairman of South African mobile telephone company Vodacom, a joint venture between Telkom and Britain's Vodafone Plc, Telkom said on Monday.</p>
<p>The resignation, effective from October 1, 1997, follows Martin's appointment as managing director-designate of Siemens Telecommunictions (Pty) Ltd, a unit of Siemens AG.</p>
<p>Martin is also stepping down from the Telkom board.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
